{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["<b>Could one be found such as this, etc.</b> The reason he did not say <b>could one be found a man in whom</b> etc. <b>such as this</b> is that then it would have sounded as though a man in whom is the spirit of Elohim could be found, only he is not similar — but that is not what he intended to say. Rather, he meant that no one of this species is to be found who has in him the spirit, etc. — neither he himself nor any fraction of him."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:47:38.282128668Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}